==Latin==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|itc-pro|la}} {{m|itc-pro|*kesdō}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{m|ine-pro|*ḱiesdʰ-||to drive away; to go away}}. Cognates include Sanskrit {{m|sa|सेधति|tr=sedhati||to drive, chase away}} and Avestan {{m|ae|𐬯𐬍𐬀𐬰𐬛𐬀𐬝||will chase away}}, from {{etyl|iir|-}} {{m|iir-pro|*ćiazd-}}, {{m|iir-pro|*ćižd-}}.<ref>{{R:De Vaan 2008|pages=103-104|head='''cēdō''', -'''ere'''}}</ref>

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|eccl=1|cēdō}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|cēdō|cēdere|cessī|cessum|conj=3}}

# {{label|la|intransitive}} I [[go]], [[move]], [[proceed]], [[go along]], [[move]] along.
# {{label|la|intransitive}} I [[result]], [[turn out]], [[happen]].
# {{label|la|intransitive}} I [[withdraw]], [[depart]], [[retire]], go away from.
## {{label|la|intransitive|military}} I withdraw, [[fall back]], [[give up]] my post.
# {{label|la|intransitive}} I [[disappear]], [[pass away]], [[vanish]].
# {{label|la|intransitive|with dative}} I [[cede]], [[give in]] or [[yield]] (to), [[step aside]] (for), [[give way]] (to).
#* [[w:Virgil|Vergilius]], [[w:Aeneid|Aeneis]], Book VI, line 95
#*: Tu ne '''cede''' malis, sed contra audentior ito
#*:: '''Give in''' not to evils, but go against them more daring.
#* Motto of Wyoming
#*: Cedant arma togae.
#*:: Let the arms concede to the toga (Let war yield to diplomacy)
## {{label|la|intransitive}} I am [[inferior]] to, yield to in rank.
# {{label|la|transitive}} I [[concede]], give up, [[grant]], [[surrender]], [[yield]].
# {{label|la|intransitive|with dative or in +acc.}} I [[fall]] (to) (as a possession); [[accrue]] or [[come]] (to).
# {{label|la|intransitive|with in +acc.}} I [[become]], [[turn into]], be or become the [[equivalent]] of.

